{"question_id": "54026fce", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Based on what's worked in our past discussions, here are some ideas:\n\n- **Virtual coffee breaks** — You already like this idea and plan to raise it at your next team meeting. Keep it regular (e.g., a set weekly slot), frame it as a collaborative suggestion, and use ground rules: no work talk, keep it light and casual, respect everyone's time, be present, use video, and rotate conversation starters.\n- **Informal chat channels** — Create or join a Slack/Microsoft Teams channel for non-work conversations (shared interests, weekend plans, pet photos, etc.) so the socializing continues between calls.\n- **Virtual games or team-building** — Try trivia, online escape rooms, or similar activities as a fun, low-pressure way to interact.\n- **Gauge interest first** — Consider sending a quick survey or raising it at a team meeting before launching anything, so people feel involved in the decision.\n- **Pick a reliable, easy-to-use video platform** — Since you want the tech to be frictionless for casual chats.\n\nThe coffee breaks plus a chat channel are probably the easiest place to start.", "n_records": 12, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1156, "completion_tokens": 439, "calls": 1}, "selected": ["self|work_from_home_preference", "self|remote_work_social_isolation", "self|virtual_coffee_break_interest", "self|team_meeting_plan", "self|virtual_coffee_break_ground_rules", "self|virtual_coffee_break_schedule", "self|video_conferencing_preference", "assistant|virtual_coffee_break_suggestion", "assistant|online_team_activities_suggestion", "assistant|social_channels_suggestion", "assistant|discuss_and_agree_suggestion", "assistant|coffee_break_ground_rules_suggestion"], "digest_bytes": 2129}
{"question_id": "09d032c9", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Based on your profile, here's what I can offer: you already own a portable power bank, which is the most direct fix for battery anxiety on the go. If your current one isn't lasting, memory lists several higher-capacity upgrades:\n\n- **Anker PowerCore 5000** — 5,000mAh, ~1.5 phone charges, $15\n- **Mophie Powerstation Mini** — 5,000mAh, ~2 phone charges, $30\n- **Jackery Titan S** — 10,000mAh, multiple USB ports, ~3 phone charges, $25\n- **Aukey Power Bank 10000mAh** — ~3 phone charges, multiple USB ports, $20\n- **Eggtronic Power Bank 10000mAh** — ~3 phone charges, USB-C included, $30\n- **Anker PowerCore Fusion** — 10,000mAh, USB-C included, ~3 phone charges, $35\n\nIf your current power bank is a small one, stepping up to a 10,000mAh model (like the Aukey at $20 or Jackery Titan S at $25) would roughly double-to-triple your away-from-outlet runtime.\n\nMemory only records your device ownership and these power bank options — it doesn't contain general battery-saving tips (screen brightness, background apps, etc.) for your specific phone.", "n_records": 49, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 2553, "completion_tokens": 756, "calls": 1}, "selected": ["self|portable_power_bank", "self|wireless_charging_pad", "self|apple_watch", "self|travel_habits", "self|tv_purchase_plan", "assistant|tech_organization_suggestion", "assistant|travel_case_option", "assistant|bellroy_tech_kit_pros", "assistant|bellroy_tech_kit_cons", "assistant|peak_design_tech_pouch_pros", "assistant|peak_design_tech_pouch_cons", "assistant|cable_organizer_option", "assistant|power_bank_option", "assistant|lg_tv_lineup", "assistant|lg_tv_deal", "assistant|lg_tv_recommendation", "assistant|lg_oled_c9_picture_quality", "assistant|lg_oled_c9_viewing_angles", "assistant|lg_oled_c9_hdr", "assistant|lg_oled_c9_processor", "assistant|lg_oled_c9_gaming", "assistant|lg_oled_c9_ai_image_enhancement", "assistant|lg_oled_c9_audio"], "di